set {BarrierDownCL} = false
audio "res://Audio/SoundEffects/Foley Toy Slam Closed Door 01.wav"
...
Virtue: Why is it so dark in here?
Using what little light I can get from the door behind me, I walk further into the room, hoping something, anything will bring off its own light.
As I walk into the room, the door closes behind me, and im bombarded with an overwhelming feeling that compels me to close my eyes
With all the strength in my being I try to keep my composure, and pry my eyes open against this force
What should I do?
- Submit to it
	Whatever this is, there's no use in fighting it.
	As I shut my eyelids I see a blue light in the distance
	Somehow even brighter now that my eyes are closed. It shines straight through to me.
	A weight of complex emotions wash over me spontaneously
	Im angry
	Im sad
	Im lost
	Im afraid
	All in one second I feel a lifetimes worth of emotions and ideas.
	I understand
	I need to calm myself, and see through these emotions
	But not to discard them, but use them like paint strokes in seeing my surroundings
	I am the canvas.
	set {BarrierDownCL} = true
- Keep fighting
	Against what feels like thousands of small hands clasping the musles of my face I push to pry my eyes open
	For what little glimpses of success I have, I stare through my eyelashes, and I see something. A blurry glimpse of blue light.
	wait, no.
	I dont see this light when I  pry my eyes
	I see them while theyre closed!
	As I aimlessly move towards this light its force strengthens, and I find myself in a losing battle
	My body feels atrophied
	Claudma: Wake up.
	set {BarrierDownCL} = true